{"name":"High Salute","hex":"#445056","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"high","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Physically elevated, extending above a base or average level:\n Very elevated; extending or being far above a base; tall; lofty.","Very elevated; extending or being far above a base; tall; lofty."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In or to an elevated position.","In or at a great value."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/high"},{"term":"salute","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An utterance or gesture expressing greeting or honor towards someone,  a formal, non-verbal gesture made with the arms or hands in any of various specific positions. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A kiss, offered in salutation."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make a gesture in honor of (someone or something).","To act in thanks, honor, or tribute; to thank or extend gratitude; to praise."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salute"}],"entries":[{"title":"Salute","blocks":[{"text":"A salute is usually a formal hand gesture or other action used to display respect in military situations. Salutes are primarily associated with the military and law enforcement, but many civilian organizations, such as Girl Guides, Boy Scouts and the Salvation Army use formal salutes. Ordinary civilians also salute informally to greet or acknowledge the presence of another person, such as a tip of the hat or a hand wave to a friend or neighbor."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Victory_Day_Parade_2005-14.jpg/330px-Victory_Day_Parade_2005-14.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salute","wikidata":"Q858893"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Firli_Bahuri_Kapolda.png/500px-Firli_Bahuri_Kapolda.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content